\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The undeclared seed: one exact throat, two resolutions, two fates. (a)~Minimal areal radius of the lone drainhole evolved from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted); each level holds it until its own truncation error excites the unstable mode, and the fate flips with the grid: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates. Level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure at $t=24.2$ (cross) with the throat still exact to $0.12\%$---too coarse to reach the branch at all. Dot and muted line as in Fig.~\ref {fig:seed_branches}: the scan loses the level-3 throat at $t=65$ while the run continues to $t=100$ behind a marginally trapped surface (areal radius $3.23\to 2.37$). (b)~The deviation grows exponentially on both grids: plateau fits over $t=49$--$61$ give e-fold times $\tau =5.88$ (level 3) and $5.26$ (level 4)---the same unstable mode to $9\%$, $T=\tau \,\alpha _{\rm  th}/R_\star =0.87$ and $0.78$ against the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band $0.68$--$0.76$~\cite  {gonzalez2009}---with opposite sign. The fate is the truncation seed's; the mode is the throat's.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:branches}{{1}{4}{The undeclared seed: one exact throat, two resolutions, two fates. (a)~Minimal areal radius of the lone drainhole evolved from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted); each level holds it until its own truncation error excites the unstable mode, and the fate flips with the grid: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates. Level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure at $t=24.2$ (cross) with the throat still exact to $0.12\%$---too coarse to reach the branch at all. Dot and muted line as in Fig.~\ref {fig:seed_branches}: the scan loses the level-3 throat at $t=65$ while the run continues to $t=100$ behind a marginally trapped surface (areal radius $3.23\to 2.37$). (b)~The deviation grows exponentially on both grids: plateau fits over $t=49$--$61$ give e-fold times $\tau =5.88$ (level 3) and $5.26$ (level 4)---the same unstable mode to $9\%$, $T=\tau \,\alpha _{\rm th}/R_\star =0.87$ and $0.78$ against the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band $0.68$--$0.76$~\cite {gonzalez2009}---with opposite sign. The fate is the truncation seed's; the mode is the throat's}{figure.1}{}}
